Article 12 An administrative license may be established for the following matters:
(1) Specific activities directly involving national security, public security, macroeconomic regulation, ecological environment protection, and directly relating to personal health and safety of life and property, for which approval is required in accordance with statutory conditions;
(2) The development and utilization of limited natural resources, allocation of public resources, and market access of specific industries directly relating to public interest, for which specific rights need to be granted;
(3) Professions and industries providing public services and directly relating to public interest, for which qualifications or credentials such as special reputation, special conditions or special skills need to be determined;
(4) Important equipment, facilities, products and articles directly relating to public security, personal health and safety of life and property, for which examination needs to be conducted through inspection, testing, quarantine, etc., in accordance with technical standards and technical specifications;
(5) The establishment of enterprises or other organizations, for which subject qualification needs to be determined; and
(6) Other matters for which administrative license may be established as provided by laws and administrative regulations.

Article 13 For the matters listed in Article 12 of this Law, if they can be regulated by the following means, no administrative license may be established:
(1) They can be decided independently by citizens, legal persons or other organizations;
(2) They can be effectively regulated by the market competition mechanism;
(3) They can be self-disciplined by trade organizations or intermediary agencies; or
(4) Administrative organs can resolve them by adopting other administrative management methods such as post-event supervision.

Article 69 In any of the following circumstances, the administrative organ that made the administrative license decision or its higher-level administrative organ may, upon the request of an interested party or ex officio, revoke the administrative license:
(1) The staff member of the administrative organ abused his or her powers or neglected his or her duties in making the decision to grant the administrative license;
(2) The decision to grant the administrative license was made beyond the statutory functions and powers;
(3) The decision to grant the administrative license was made in violation of statutory procedures;
(4) The administrative license was granted to an applicant who did not have the qualifications to apply or did not meet the statutory conditions;
(5) Other circumstances under which the administrative license may be revoked according to law.
Where a licensee obtains an administrative license by improper means such as deception or bribery, the license shall be revoked.
If revoking the administrative license in accordance with the preceding two paragraphs may cause significant damage to the public interest, the license shall not be revoked.
Where an administrative license is revoked in accordance with paragraph 1 of this Article, if the lawful rights and interests of the licensee are damaged, the administrative organ shall provide compensation according to law. Where an administrative license is revoked in accordance with paragraph 2 of this Article, the interests obtained by the licensee based on the administrative license shall not be protected.

Article 70 An administrative organ shall go through the cancellation formalities for the relevant administrative license according to law under any of the following circumstances:
(1) The term of validity of the administrative license expires without renewal;
(2) The administrative license granting a specific qualification to a citizen is issued and the citizen dies or loses the capacity for civil conduct;
(3) The legal person or other organization terminates according to law;
(4) The administrative license is revoked or withdrawn according to law, or the administrative license certificate is revoked according to law;
(5) The matter of the administrative license cannot be implemented due to force majeure;
(6) Other circumstances under which the administrative license shall be cancelled as provided for by laws or regulations.

Article 72 Where an administrative organ or its staff member violates the provisions of this Law and falls under any of the following circumstances, the administrative organ at the higher level or the supervisory organ shall order it to make corrections; if the circumstances are serious, the persons directly in charge and other persons directly responsible shall be given administrative sanctions according to law:
(1) Failing to accept an application for administrative license that meets the statutory conditions;
(2) Failing to disclose at the place of business the materials that shall be disclosed according to law;
(3) Failing to perform the statutory obligation to inform the applicant or interested party during the process of acceptance, review, and decision on the administrative license;
(4) Failing to inform the applicant at one time of all the contents that must be supplemented or corrected when the application materials submitted by the applicant are incomplete or do not conform to the statutory form;
(5) Illegally disclosing the trade secrets, undisclosed information, or confidential business information submitted by the applicant;
(6) Making the transfer of technology a condition for obtaining the administrative license, or directly or indirectly requiring the transfer of technology during the implementation of the administrative license;
(7) Failing to explain the reasons for not accepting an application for administrative license or for not granting the administrative license according to law;
(8) Failing to hold a hearing when it shall be held according to law.

Article 74 Where an administrative organ falls under any of the following circumstances in implementing an administrative license, the administrative organ at the higher level or the supervisory organ shall order it to make corrections, and the persons directly in charge and other persons directly responsible shall be given administrative sanctions according to law; if the act constitutes a crime, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law:
(1) Granting an administrative license to an applicant who does not meet the statutory conditions or making a decision to grant an administrative license beyond the statutory authority;
(2) Failing to grant an administrative license to an applicant who meets the statutory conditions or failing to make a decision to grant an administrative license within the statutory time limit;
(3) Making a decision to grant an administrative license according to the results of bid invitation, auction, or examination scores where it is required by law to select the best candidate, but failing to conduct bid invitation, auction, or examination, or failing to make a decision based on the results of bid invitation, auction, or examination scores.

Article 80 Where a licensee commits any of the following acts, the administrative organ shall impose an administrative penalty according to law; if the act constitutes a crime, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law:
(1) Altering, reselling, leasing, lending out the administrative license certificate, or illegally transferring the administrative license in other forms;
(2) Engaging in activities beyond the scope of the administrative license;
(3) Concealing relevant information, providing false materials, or refusing to provide truthful materials reflecting its activities to the administrative organ responsible for supervision and inspection;
(4) Other illegal acts provided for by laws, regulations, or rules.
